# A `match` whose value is taken must match every value.
#
# A `match` that fits no arm does nothing (PYKING.md), so one whose
# value is being bound has to be unable to fit nothing -- otherwise the
# type reported for `label` names a value that need never exist, and
# the name is simply not there at run time.
#
# The statement form is unaffected: it may match nothing and do nothing.
# What makes this one different is the `=`.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.ast.out` holds
# the error message, not a program's output.

def label(n:Int) -> String:
    text = match n:
        case 0: "zero"
        case 1: "one"
    return text
